P = {
# ── caloric_math: Resource Command escalates who gets cut ──
"quest_caloric_math_01": ("Resource Command has flagged minor offenders as a caloric liability. The arithmetic is printed at the bottom: cut their rations by a third and the surplus holds through winter. The memo is signed, which is new.",
 "The cookhouse steward stands in the ration line with the memo in one hand and the ladle in the other, moving neither.",
 "Cut the offenders' rations by a third.", "Burn the memo. Serve full plates."),
"quest_caloric_math_02": ("The next memo names the unemployed: anyone without an assignment burns calories the shelter cannot replace. The list has nine names. Three of them lost their postings when the workshop flooded, and the memo does not mention why.",
 "Nine people stand at the back of the ration line, watching the ladle stop short of their bowls.",
 "Cut the unassigned to half rations.", "Find them work instead."),
"quest_caloric_math_03": ("Resource Command has started counting birth years. Everyone over sixty eats eight percent of the stores and produces nothing, and the arithmetic is neat, and the handwriting gets more careful with each memo, as if the author is trying not to think about it.",
 "The eldest dweller, eighty-one, holds out his bowl the way he always has. The server looks at the tally board instead of him.",
 "Reduce the rations of the over-sixties.", "Take the cut from Command's own table."),
"quest_caloric_math_04": ("The sick are flagged next: fevers burn calories, and the infirmary line now costs double what it cost in autumn. The memo proposes thinning their soup until the stores stop bleeding. Someone has penciled in the savings already.",
 "The infirmary cook tastes the thinned batch and sets the spoon down very carefully, the way you set down something that might break.",
 "Thin the infirmary rations.", "Feed the sick first. Absorb the deficit."),
"quest_caloric_math_05": ("The memo now distinguishes the injured from the sick, because paperwork distinguishes. Anyone healing takes a reduced plate until they return to duty. The list is longer than expected, because nobody wanted to be the one who reported a wound.",
 "A man with a splinted arm reads his own name on the cookhouse door, then quietly rolls his sleeve down over the splint.",
 "Halve rations until they heal.", "Strike the list. Feed them whole."),
"quest_caloric_math_06": ("The memo has reached the children's dormitory. Orphans take rations without a household to offset the cost, and Resource Command proposes folding their plates into the general deficit. The word orphan appears in the arithmetic like a line item.",
 "The dormitory matron stands in the doorway with the census sheet behind her back, and she is not handing it over.",
 "Cut the orphans' hall to half.", "Refuse. The children eat."),
"quest_caloric_math_07": ("Resource Command has noticed that the grieving eat poorly, and proposes to help with that: anyone filed under recent loss takes a reduced plate, and the office calls this a kindness twice. The list is mostly women.",
 "The grief register was a courtesy once. Now it is a ration list, and people have started to notice.",
 "File the grieving as dependents.", "Close the register to Command."),
"quest_caloric_math_08": ("The arithmetic has turned upside down: the pregnant cost more now and may not repay it, says the margin note, and their supplement is to be cut. The clerk who wrote the memo requested a transfer the next morning. It was denied.",
 "The clinic nurse has taped the supplement schedule to the door where everyone can see it, in letters large enough to be a dare.",
 "Cut the supplements.", "Double them. Feed them both."),
"quest_caloric_math_09": ("Resource Command has stopped naming categories and started using a scale. Anyone under the weight threshold is marked W and eats reduced until they become economically viable. The scale stands at the cookhouse door, and nobody wants to be first to step on it.",
 "The line stops at the scale. Someone has chalked a mark on the wall beside it, higher than anyone can reach.",
 "Enforce the weight line.", "Move the scale to the scrap room."),
"quest_caloric_math_10": ("The final memo addresses everyone: the production figures are in, the lowest tenth of producers eat reduced until output improves, and the list is posted at every door. Yesterday it was the lowest tenth. The memos no longer propose. They ask how long you intend to keep saying no.",
 "The settlement stands before the posted list, reading it in a silence that has weight.",
 "Post the list. Enforce it.", "Tear the list down. The cookhouse stays open."),
# ── oxygen_triage: Engineering cuts circulation as fuel fails ──
"quest_oxygen_triage_01": ("The fuel gauge slipped another notch and Engineering has done the arithmetic aloud: cutting oxygen circulation to Storage Sector C during the night shift buys nine more days of power. Nothing sleeps in storage. That is the entire argument.",
 "The valve wheel for Sector C has a tag on it now, and the tag has tonight's date on it.",
 "Shut the valve on Sector C.", "Burn furniture for fuel instead. Keep the air."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_02": ("Engineering's report is shorter each time. The recreation deck loses circulation during the night shift and the fuel lasts another week. The deck is where the settlement plays cards, teaches, and holds its funerals, and none of those happen in daylight anymore.",
 "Someone left a deck of cards on the valve wheel. No one has moved either of them.",
 "Cut the deck's air at night.", "Cut the lights instead. Keep the deck."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_03": ("The report names Dormitory 4 now: forty-one sleepers, night shift only. Engineering promises the carbon buildup stays tolerable if the sleepers keep still. The forty-one have been asked, politely, not to move much in their sleep.",
 "The door of Dormitory 4 is open, and its people sit on their bunks waiting to hear what has been decided.",
 "Throttle Dormitory 4.", "Move the sleepers out. Double up elsewhere."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_04": ("Dormitory 3 is next on the list, and the people in it know the pattern: the air thins one door at a time. The engineer who signed the report sleeps in Dormitory 3, and he has asked that the cut start with his own bunk, and he means it.",
 "The engineer stands at the manifold with his wrench, waiting for the order he wrote.",
 "Cut Dormitory 3 as planned.", "Refuse. Find the fuel first."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_05": ("The report reaches the infirmary annex, and this time the engineer has not signed it. The annex holds the people who breathe hardest, and the fuel it saves is spent somewhere else, on people who can afford it least. The memo requests a decision by lights-out.",
 "The charge nurse has taped a copy of the report to the clinic door, next to the patient count.",
 "Cut the annex circulation.", "Cut Command's lighting circuits instead."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_06": ("Nobody will sign the nursery memo. It sits on the council table with its arithmetic: circulation to the nursery can throttle for six night hours and the fuel lasts a month longer. The children are small, the report notes. They need less.",
 "The nursery door is closed, and behind it someone is singing, low, to keep from hearing the meeting.",
 "Throttle the nursery's air.", "Burn every chair before that valve shuts."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_07": ("The memo moves to hydroponics: the maintenance crew's bay can run on stale air during the night shift, and the plants will not notice until morning, by which time the numbers will have improved. The crew chief has written a one-line reply: plants notice everything.",
 "The hydroponics chief waits in the council doorway with her crew behind her, arms folded.",
 "Cut the bay's circulation.", "Side with the chief. Keep the bay breathing."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_08": ("The report no longer names rooms. General population takes a universal night reduction: thin air for everyone, which the engineer says is fair and also says will kill the weakest by morning. The settlement has noticed these two facts do not sit together.",
 "Every door in the shelter carries the same notice now, and every door stands open.",
 "Thin the air for everyone.", "Ration the fuel, not the breath."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_09": ("Command's proposal is one page: the command deck keeps full circulation, and the rest of the shelter breathes on the reduced schedule. The memo calls this triage. It does not say what is being triaged for, and nobody on the council wants to ask, which is the worst part.",
 "Someone polished the valve handle on the command deck's air line. Nobody remembers who.",
 "Cut everything below Command.", "Open Command's valves to the whole shelter."),
"quest_oxygen_triage_10": ("The last report is one paragraph. Sealing circulation to the entire lower level saves the generator: everyone above breathes, everyone below does not, and the word evacuate appears once, in parentheses, like an afterthought. There are sixty people down there. The number is on the last line.",
 "Sixty people have come up and stand in the common hall, quietly, carrying what they could hold.",
 "Seal the lower level.", "Kill the generator. Everyone breathes together."),
# ── medical_attrition: the dispensary is stripped for the elite ──
"quest_medical_attrition_01": ("An order has come down to the dispensary: painkillers are to be withheld and stockpiled for elite personnel. The medical officer has been asked to count what remains, and she has counted twice, and the number came out lower the second time, and nobody knows why.",
 "The dispensary shelf has been rearranged so the empty spaces face the wall.",
 "Lock up the painkillers.", "Give them to whoever hurts."),
"quest_medical_attrition_02": ("The second order names bandages. Clean cloth goes to the command infirmary first, and the rest of the shelter learns to boil and reuse. The laundry nurse has started keeping a separate tally: wounds reopened, counted at the end of each shift.",
 "A line of re-used bandages hangs drying above the boiler. They never come back white.",
 "Seize the bandage stock.", "Refuse. Tear the sheets if you must."),
"quest_medical_attrition_03": ("The order names antibiotics now, and the medical officer has begun lying a little on the inventory forms, each day, so the shelves look emptier than they are. She has told nobody about this. She has told one person. It is in this report.",
 "The locked cabinet has two padlocks on it now, and the two keys are kept by different people.",
 "Stockpile for Command.", "Prescribe freely. Cross out the order."),
"quest_medical_attrition_04": ("Antiseptics are next, and the order includes a justification this time: elite personnel face greater risk and require priority dosing. The clinic has been asked to dilute what remains for general use. What remains is already diluted.",
 "The clinic smells of boiled water now, where it used to smell of iodine.",
 "Dilute and hand it over.", "Keep the bottles. Mark them clinic-only."),
"quest_medical_attrition_05": ("The order names surgical thread. The medical officer has replied with a list of the wounds closed this month with wire, tape, and glue, and sent it up through channels unsigned. The reply came back with the same order, and a pen for her signature.",
 "The pen sits on her desk next to the order, and neither has been touched all day.",
 "Sign and comply.", "Break the pen. Keep the thread."),
"quest_medical_attrition_06": ("The order reaches anesthesia: operations below command priority are to be performed without it, and the directive says patients recover better when they remember the cost. The medical officer has posted next week's surgery schedule on the door, unedited.",
 "The settlement has started reading the surgery schedule like weather. Tomorrow has three entries.",
 "Operate without anesthesia.", "Use the stock. Take the consequences."),
"quest_medical_attrition_07": ("The directive names blood now. Transfusions are reserved for elite personnel, and the clinic is asked to maintain a donor list for the purpose. The first volunteer sheet went up this morning. Every name on it is crossed out, and the crossings-out are in different hands.",
 "The donor sheet hangs by the clinic door, crossed out, and nobody has taken it down.",
 "Enforce the donor list.", "Burn the list."),
"quest_medical_attrition_08": ("The order has reached the dying: life support is to be freed for elite priority cases. The clinic holds four people who cannot be moved, and the directive calls them low-yield, and the medical officer has asked, in writing, what that word means. There is no reply.",
 "Four beds, four breath machines, and a memo on the wall with the words low-yield circled in pencil.",
 "Pull the machines.", "Bar the door. Let them breathe."),
"quest_medical_attrition_09": ("The directive names comfort now. Palliative care is suspended; the morphine is already gone; the dying are to be kept clean and quiet on what remains. The hospice volunteers have been asked to attend a briefing on compassionate efficiency. None of them went.",
 "The briefing room sits empty. Down the hall, someone is singing to a man who is dying.",
 "Cut care to the minimum.", "Keep the vigils. Ignore the order."),
"quest_medical_attrition_10": ("The final directive is almost gentle: all non-essential treatment is suspended until further notice, and the definition of essential is attached, and it is shorter than anyone feared and longer than anyone hoped. The medical officer has read it three times and started answering patients anyway.",
 "The dispensary door stands open, the directive posted beside it, and the line of patients goes past both.",
 "Enforce the definition.", "Treat everyone. Send Command the bill."),
# ── disciplinary_iron: penalties climb into absurdity ──
"quest_disciplinary_iron_01": ("A new order has been posted by the ration line: complaints about rations are now a physical offense, and the word used is corrective. The incident sheet has its first name on it, and it is the woman who asked about the beans.",
 "The incident sheet has been up one day, and it has one name, and the ration line reads it while it waits.",
 "Post the order. Enforce it.", "Take the sheet down. Listen instead."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_02": ("The order has moved to the workshop: resting on shift is now theft of output, and theft of output is punished in the yard. The foreman asked for the definition of rest, in writing. It arrived. It includes sitting down.",
 "A worker leans against the wall with his eyes closed, and two men are watching to see what happens next.",
 "Enforce the yard penalty.", "Build rest into the rota instead."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_03": ("The order names feeling now. Crying in public lowers morale, and lowered morale is an offense, and the offense is corrected physically and promptly. Nobody has defined promptly. The mess hall has gone very quiet at meals.",
 "A woman cries at the third table with her napkin over her face, and everyone nearby looks away on purpose.",
 "Enforce the order.", "Refuse. Grief is not an offense."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_04": ("The settlement is allowed two hours of official mourning per death, and the new order penalizes mourning off-schedule as unauthorized assembly. Yesterday's funeral ran long because the grave was frozen, and the mourners have been summoned to explain themselves.",
 "Eleven mourners stand outside the order office wearing their grave-clothes.",
 "Enforce the schedule.", "Let the funeral take its time."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_05": ("The order has reached its point: questioning orders is now verbal sabotage, corrected in the yard. Questions remain permitted, the notice says, provided they do not imply disagreement. The settlement is slowly working out the difference, in whispers.",
 "The notice hangs in six places. Someone has penciled a question mark at the bottom of one, and then erased it.",
 "Enforce the classification.", "Strike it. Questions stay free."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_06": ("The penalty for stealing food has been raised from restitution to physical correction, and the first case is a twelve-year-old who took bread from the cookhouse. The cook refused to file the complaint, so the order office filed it for him.",
 "The boy sits outside the order office with the loaf in his lap, still wrapped, uneaten.",
 "Carry out the penalty.", "Feed him. Dismiss the complaint."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_07": ("The order now reads minor: small insubordinations draw the yard, and small is defined by whoever writes the report. One man was corrected for a shrug. One woman for a sigh. The reports have started competing with each other, and the people writing them are starting to enjoy it, which is the thing to watch.",
 "The incident reports are getting longer. Today's winner is four pages, about a look.",
 "Let the reports stand.", "Burn the report box."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_08": ("The order has found its floor: injuries sustained by accident now draw a penalty, because an accident is carelessness and carelessness is sabotage, and the logic is printed at the bottom of the notice in small text. A man broke his wrist in the press yesterday. He has been asked to report for correction.",
 "The man holds his splinted wrist with his good hand and waits, politely, by the yard gate.",
 "Correct the accident.", "Fix the press. Heal the wrist."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_09": ("The quota has been raised and the penalty attached to it: missed quotas draw the yard, and the quota has been set so that three work crews will miss it by design, because someone has decided fear produces better than bread. The arithmetic is at the bottom of the notice. It does not work.",
 "Three crews have been marched to the yard at once, and the yard was not built for three crews.",
 "Hold the quota.", "Lower the quota. Close the yard."),
"quest_disciplinary_iron_10": ("The final order is posted and nobody laughs, which is how you know it is broken: heavy breathing is now a punishable offense, classified as unauthorized consumption of shared air, and the notice is signed and stamped and filed, and completely serious. Someone will enforce it. Someone always does.",
 "The notice hangs. The line reads it in silence. Nobody laughs. Nobody breathes hard either.",
 "Enforce the order.", "Tear it down. This is where it stops."),
# ── labor_extraction: shifts climb to the death-shift ──
"quest_labor_extraction_01": ("The schedule has been reissued: ten-hour shifts across all working sectors, because production lags the viability curve. The curve is a line drawn by the overseer's office, and nobody has seen the math behind it, and the schedule does not say when the line will be satisfied.",
 "The new rota is posted over the old one, and the old one is still legible underneath.",
 "Mandate the ten-hour shift.", "Hold at eight. Meet the curve another way."),
"quest_labor_extraction_02": ("The curve is still unsatisfied, so the shift is twelve hours now, and the notice includes a list of efficiencies: meals taken at the bench, tools issued once per day. The first day of the new rota has ended, and the settlement's evenings are gone, and people stand in doorways not knowing what to do with nothing.",
 "The workshop lights stay on past dark now, and the mess hall serves dinner at hours nobody calls dinner.",
 "Hold the twelve-hour shift.", "Roll it back. Rest is production too."),
"quest_labor_extraction_03": ("Fourteen hours. The schedule has been simplified to fit the page, and the page is posted everywhere, and the word temporary appears at the top in smaller letters each time it is reprinted. The infirmary has started counting accidents by hour of shift. The count climbs at hour eleven.",
 "The infirmary's accident chart hangs by the clinic door. The eleventh hour is circled.",
 "Enforce fourteen hours.", "Stop at twelve. Read the injury count aloud."),
"quest_labor_extraction_04": ("Sixteen hours now, and the schedule calls sleep maintenance downtime, which is a phrase from the overseer's office. People sleep at their benches in twenty-minute allotments, officially. The workshop floors have taken on a smell of bodies and machine oil that does not leave.",
 "Rows of sleepers at their machines in twenty-minute allotments, and a foreman walking the rows with a clock.",
 "Hold the sixteen-hour shift.", "Refuse. Nobody works sixteen hours."),
"quest_labor_extraction_05": ("The reissue has taken the weekends: seven days on, because the curve does not rest, and the notice says weekends are a pre-war luxury, and the settlement has noticed the notice never says when the curve will sleep either. The mess hall calendar still has weekends marked on it.",
 "Someone keeps marking weekends on the calendar in pencil, every week, and nobody admits to it.",
 "Abolish the weekend.", "Keep the seventh day. Hold it anyway."),
"quest_labor_extraction_06": ("The order has found the last soft place: sleep breaks are unlogged downtime, and unlogged downtime is theft, and the schedule now runs until the work is done each day, and the work is never done. The first man to drop was carried to the infirmary, and his shift was asked to account for the hours.",
 "The shift log shows a man who worked thirty-one hours, and the log has been entered into evidence against him.",
 "Strike the sleep breaks.", "Let them sleep. The work will wait."),
"quest_labor_extraction_07": ("The curve wants hands, and the order has noticed the children: anyone tall enough to reach a bench is old enough to work one, and the notice calls them junior auxiliaries, and the schoolroom has been emptied into the workshop. The teacher stands in the doorway and has not moved all morning.",
 "The children have been given stools to reach the benches, and the stools came from the schoolroom.",
 "Put the children to work.", "Empty the workshop. School continues."),
"quest_labor_extraction_08": ("The order has moved down the ages: everyone over sixty is now reserve labor, and reserve labor is not optional, and the first crew has been set to sorting salvage because their hands are patient. The oldest of them helped build the shelter's first wall. He has been given a wire brush.",
 "The elders' crew works slow and perfect, and the quota sheet does not know how to count them.",
 "Mandate the elders.", "Exempt them. Their hands are owed."),
"quest_labor_extraction_09": ("The order has reached the clinic's list: the pregnant are assigned light labor, and light labor is defined as whatever remains, and the clinic has objected in writing and the objection has been filed. The listed women have been told to report tomorrow. The clinic has told them to rest.",
 "Two instructions hang on the same door, and the settlement has started reading both, slowly.",
 "Enforce the assignment.", "Stand with the clinic. They rest."),
"quest_labor_extraction_10": ("The final schedule is posted and the settlement stands in front of it without moving: continuous shifts, no relief, until the curve is met, and the curve is not a number anymore, the curve is a word for whatever is left. Someone has written death-shifts at the bottom of the notice, and nobody has crossed it out, because it is accurate.",
 "The notice has been up for a day, and no one has signed up for the first shift, and the quota office is waiting.",
 "Open the death-shifts.", "Shut the board down. Not this."),
# ── surveillance_state: the listening spreads everywhere ──
"quest_surveillance_state_01": ("Security reports that talk is leaking, so the wires are going up in the common areas first, and the notice calls it community assurance, and the men installing the microphones are polite and ask for the best places to mount them, and half the settlement helps them.",
 "The little black microphones have gone up in the halls, and people have started talking toward them on purpose, like visitors.",
 "Wire the common areas.", "Pull them down. Trust is security too."),
"quest_surveillance_state_02": ("The wires have moved into the workshops, because leaks happen where people talk, and people talk where they work. The foreman has been asked to list who sits next to whom, and he has submitted a list, and the list is wrong on purpose, and Security knows it is wrong, and that is the part nobody says.",
 "A microphone hangs above the foreman's bench, and he has started giving his shift report to it, formally.",
 "Wire the benches.", "Refuse the seating list. Keep the benches clean."),
"quest_surveillance_state_03": ("The mess hall is wired now, because meals are where people gather, and gathering is where talk happens, and the notice says the listening is passive. The settlement has invented a new custom: tap the table twice before saying anything that matters. Everyone learned it in a day.",
 "The tables tap twice in unison all through the meals, like rain, and whoever listens must be going mad.",
 "Keep the mess hall wired.", "Strip the wires out of the walls."),
"quest_surveillance_state_04": ("The wires have reached the dormitories, and the notice says sleep is private but talk is not, and the installers have been asked to mount the microphones high, out of reach. Someone has hung a child's sock on one. It has not been taken down, and nobody knows if Security has noticed.",
 "A row of microphones, each one high on the wall, and one of them wearing a sock. The dormitory watches to see what happens.",
 "Wire the dormitories.", "Bar the installers at the door."),
"quest_surveillance_state_05": ("The order reaches the infirmary: patients talk in pain, and talk in pain is honest, so the beds get wires. The charge nurse has been asked to sign the installation form, and instead she has posted the patient list on the door with a note: these are the people you will be listening to.",
 "The patient list hangs on the clinic door with ages beside the names, and the youngest is nine, and the installers have not come back yet.",
 "Wire the beds.", "Refuse. The clinic stays clean."),
"quest_surveillance_state_06": ("The microphones are smaller now, the notice says, and private bunks are no longer exempt, and the word private has been formally removed from the housing register. The settlement has started holding its real conversations outside, in the ash, and the walks have become a custom nobody explains.",
 "Every evening, pairs walk out past the wire line into the ash and stand talking, and the watch has started calling it church.",
 "Bug the bunks.", "Burn the register's definition."),
"quest_surveillance_state_07": ("The order has reached the last rooms. Bathrooms are to be wired because conversations happen where people let their guard down, and the notice does not flinch from the word. The settlement has stopped using the rooms in pairs, and started singing in them, loudly, which is either defiance or madness.",
 "Behind the bathroom doors, all day, loud tuneless singing, and the microphones are installed anyway.",
 "Wire the last rooms.", "Smash the microphones. There is a line."),
"quest_surveillance_state_08": ("The reports no longer concern places; they concern volume. Whispered conversation is now classified as concealed speech, and concealed speech is to be reported by whoever hears it. The first report was filed yesterday. The reporter and the reported share a bunk, and neither slept last night.",
 "Two men share a bunk and have stopped speaking to each other since the report, and the settlement watches both of them.",
 "Classify the whispers.", "Burn the report. Unfile it."),
"quest_surveillance_state_09": ("The order reaches sleep. Talking in one's sleep is now unwitting testimony, and the dormitories are to keep night-logs of what is said, and the first log has been filed, and it is mostly dreams, and one man's dead wife's name appears in it eleven times, in five different hands.",
 "The night-log sits on the order office desk, and it is mostly dreams, and nobody wants to be the one to file the next one.",
 "Log the sleep-talking.", "Refuse. Sleep is the last country."),
"quest_surveillance_state_10": ("The final proposal is filed and it has a name, Total Observability, and it means what it says: every room, every voice, every hour, watched and recorded, because the leak was never found, and the office has concluded the leak is the settlement itself. The order office has asked for a vote, and the voting is being recorded, which answers the question.",
 "The proposal sits on the table, and the room knows it is being recorded, and every face has gone careful.",
 "Approve Total Observability.", "Vote no. On the record."),
}
